},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO4ScanV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Scan","text":"Scan","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"T","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"T","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"initialResult","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The initial accumulated value to start with."}]}]},{"name":"nextPartialResult","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A closure that takes the current accumulated value and the next element from the upstream sequence,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and returns a new accumulated value asynchronously.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An asynchronous sequence that produces each intermediate accumulated result."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This operator works similarly to Combine’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"scan"},{"text":" operator. It produces a sequence of values by repeatedly combining a running","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accumulated value with each new element from the upstream async sequence using the provided closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is useful for computing running totals, aggregating state, or applying stateful transformations over time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Example","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Example"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The following example demonstrates accumulating a running sum over an asynchronous sequence of integers:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ An async sequence producing the numbers 1 through 5","let numbers = AsyncStream<Int> { continuation in","    for i in 1...5 {","        continuation.yield(i)","    }","    continuation.finish()","}","","\/\/ Use scan to accumulate a running sum","let runningSum = numbers.scan(0) { partialSum, nextNumber in","    return partialSum + nextNumber","}","","\/\/ Consume the running sums","Task {","    for try await sum in runningSum {","        print(sum) \/\/ Prints: 1, 3, 6, 10, 15","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent":{"title":"Afluent","type":"topic","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/afluent"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences/Scan":{"url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/asyncsequences\/scan","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Scan","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Scan"}],"title":"AsyncSequences.Scan","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Scan"}]},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/AsyncSequences":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"AsyncSequences","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AsyncSequences","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract"